    {
      "title": "US officials decide against backing Saudi Arabia in Yemen after meeting Houthi leaders",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/us-officials-decide-against-backing-saudi-arabia-yemen-meeting-houthi-leaders",
      "description": "<p>Armed group appears to reach agreement with Trump administration over safety of Red Sea shipping</p><p>Officials from the US met Houthi leaders over the weekend at the country’s embassy in Muscat, Oman, it has been confirmed, leading to the US decision not to intervene to help Saudi Arabia drive back a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/10/violence-erupts-in-yemen-again-why-it-matters-globally-and-how-it-is-linked-to-the-us-iran-war\">Houthi advance inside Yemen</a>.</p><p>The Houthis reassured the US that the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/06/us-to-halt-bombing-campaign-against-houthis-in-yemen-trump-says\">ceasefire agreement between the two sides</a> struck in 2025 still held and the movement had no intention of attacking US shipping in the Red Sea. Only Saudi-linked shipping was regarded as a target owing to its blockade of Yemen, the Houthis confirmed.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/us-officials-decide-against-backing-saudi-arabia-yemen-meeting-houthi-leaders\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T14:56:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saudi Arabia warns of ‘red line’ after Houthi drone intercepted close to holy city of Mecca",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/saudi-arabia-houthi-drone-shot-down-mecca-iran-middle-east",
      "description": "<p>Iran-aligned group rejects claim it targeted Mecca, while Organisation of Islamic Cooperation condemns attack</p><p>Saudi Arabia has claimed its air defences intercepted and destroyed a ⁠Houthi drone attempting to fly over the holy city of Mecca, as Saudi warplanes continued to pound Yemen, raising fears of the conflict spreading further across the Middle East.</p><p>The Saudi-led military coalition said the security of Mecca – home to Islam’s two holiest sites – was a “red line” and that it would take necessary measures against the ⁠Houthis.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/16/saudi-arabia-houthi-drone-shot-down-mecca-iran-middle-east\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T02:56:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Houthis and Saudis Trade Claims of Military Attacks as Conflict Escalates",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/16/world/middleeast/saudi-arabia-houthi-fighter-jet-mecca-drone.html",
      "description": "The Iran-backed militia in Yemen said it had downed a Saudi jet, while the Saudi-led military coalition accused it of firing a drone near Mecca. The Houthis denied doing so.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-09-16T15:26:21"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saudi Arabia says it shot down Houthi drone near Mecca, Houthis deny claim",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/saudi-arabia-houthi-drone-mecca-attack-denial-126091600182_1.html",
      "description": "Riyadh says the drone was intercepted south of Mecca before entering restricted airspace, while the Houthis deny targeting the holy city as fighting with Saudi-backed forces intensifies",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-16T04:18:27"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saudi says Houthis targeted Mecca with a drone, Iran-backed group rejects claim",
